      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #27, 2026-08-11):
      ⍝ lrm p.278-279: "Executes R. If R fails or is interrupted,
      ⍝ executes L." A branch inside R that lands outside its caller's
      ⍝ own range (here: immediate execution, so any →N is "outside")
      ⍝ must fall back to L, per lrm p.349 Figure 38 ("0 or any other
      ⍝ line number not within the function... flow of execution
      ⍝ returns to the invoking expression"). handle_QUAD_ES_BRA()
      ⍝ (Prefix.cc) used to just discard StateIndicator::jump()'s
      ⍝ result instead of acting on it, silently dropping the branch.
      ⍝
      Z←'3×2' ⎕EA '→0'
      Z
6

      ⍝ regression: L, executed as the fallback, itself failing with a
      ⍝ real error is handled correctly (handle_QUAD_ES_ERR).
      ⍝
      Z←'!¯3' ⎕EA '!¯5'
DOMAIN ERROR
      !¯3
      ^

      →

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #27, 2026-08-11):
      ⍝ R fails, falls back to L, and L itself is a branch with nowhere
      ⍝ real to go (immediate execution, no suspended function) -- lrm
      ⍝ p.349 Figure 38 says this means "flow of execution returns to
      ⍝ the invoking expression", i.e. a clean, valueless completion,
      ⍝ not an error. Bif_F1_EXECUTE::execute_statement('→0') pushes a
      ⍝ real )SI for the branch (unlike a foldable value expression);
      ⍝ that )SI is now marked via StateIndicator::set_void_on_orphan_
      ⍝ branch() so Command.cc's ordinarily-correct "→N without
      ⍝ function" SYNTAX ERROR check treats it as void instead.
      ⍝
      '→0' ⎕EA 'Z←!¯3'
      1+1
2

      ⍝ regression: the fallback L branching to a REAL, in-range label
      ⍝ of the calling function must still work normally (confirms the
      ⍝ new void-on-orphan-branch marker only fires when there is truly
      ⍝ nothing to resume into, not whenever L happens to be a branch).
      ⍝
